---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FeedbackWidget from '../components/FeedbackWidget.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---
<Layout title="Ship with AI">
  <h1>Ship with AI: Review, Secure, and Deploy with Confidence</h1>
  <p>
    AI writes more code, faster than ever. That's the easy part. The hard part — the part that
    decides whether shipping with AI is safe — is what happens next: who reviews it, who secures
    it, and how it gets from a pull request to production without anyone's attention slipping.
  </p>
  <p>
    This site is both things at once. It's the companion material for AI Genius Season 5,
    Episode 3, and a rehearsal repository for reviewing, securing, and deploying a small site.
    Automatic code review has been demonstrated separately; Issue → cloud agent and Agent Merge
    are not yet verified. This safe version uses an approved manual merge, not a claimed automated fix-and-merge.
  </p>
  <div class="card">
    <strong>The trust gap.</strong> The more code an AI assistant produces, the more your review,
    security, and release process has to carry. Speed without those guardrails just moves risk
    downstream — into your dependencies, your CI/CD pipeline, and your production environment.
  </div>
  <h2>Where to start</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={`${base}pipeline/`}>The pipeline</a> — how an idea becomes a deployed change</li>
    <li><a href={`${base}secure-supply-chain/`}>Secure your supply chain</a> — the security spine of this demo</li>
    <li><a href={`${base}diy/`}>Do it yourself</a> — plan the setup for your own repo</li>
  </ul>
  <FeedbackWidget />
</Layout>
